The West Kowloon Cultural District Authority welcomes exceptional talent with a passion to realise the vision and mission of making the West Kowloon Cultural District a prime local and international destination for arts, culture and entertainment.
(This is 18\\\\-month fixed\\\\-term contract)
The role will collaborate closely with business units, IT teams, and external vendors to ensure the effective delivery and optimisation of a new ERP solution. This role focuses on analysing business processes, enhancing system functionality, and driving integration initiatives to support operational excellence.
You will be responsible for:* facilitating communication and collaboration between users, IT teams and vendors to ensure successful project delivery;
* conducting a thorough analysis of business and system flows to identify opportunities for improvement with documentation;
* participating in cross\\\\-team development to ensure interfaces and system integrations are up to standard;
* working with the infrastructure team to ensure the systems and applications are running with the expected environment setup;
* liaising with external service providers to ensure the applications and operations comply with IT policies and standards;
* participating in system testing, user acceptance testing, and change management activities to ensure smooth implementation and user adoption;
* providing training and routine support on systems and processes to end users; and
* performing any other duties from time to time as reasonably assigned by the Authority.


You should:* possess a Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, Business Administration, or equivalent;
* have at least 5 years of experience as an IT Business Analyst, System Analyst, or in a similar role;
* have experience in managing and implementing Oracle Fusion (Finance or Procurement module) is an advantage;
* have strong analytical and problem\\\\-solving skills, with the ability to translate business requirements into technical specifications;
* have a solid understanding of software development methodologies and project management principles;
* have proven vendor management experience with good relationships;
* be a proven team player with a mature and positive attitude; and
* be proficient in spoken and written English and Chinese. Proficiency in Mandarin is an advantage.


For interested parties, please submit your application with detailed CV on or before following date. Applicants are encouraged to submit their applications as soon as possible. The review of applications will continue until post is filled.
20\\\\-11\\\\-2025
Data collected will only be used for job application processing. Your data may be accessed by our appointed recruitment consultants who have agreed to keep confidence of all personal data in not less than the standards applicable to us. Applicants not being invited for interview within 4 weeks from the submission date may assume their applications unsuccessful.
All related information will be kept up to 24 months and all personal data will be destroyed afterwards.
For more information, please visit https://www.westk.hk or contact:
Jason Wong /\\\\+852 22000285

The Property Management Services Authority (PMSA) is the statutory body established under the Property Management Services Ordinance (Cap 626\\\\) and is tasked to regulate and promote the development of the property management industry. For further details about the PMSA, please visit website at www.pmsa.org.hk.



Responsibilities



Reporting to the Senior Manager (Complaints and Enforcement) or Senior Manager (Licensing), the appointee will be responsible for the following:



Transfer data from hard copy to a digital database;



Review data for deficiencies or errors and make any necessary changes to records;



Assist with license applications or complaints that require large amount of data entry;



Provide occasional clerical and administrative support and;



Undertake ad\\\\-hoc tasks as assigned from time to time.



Requirements



HKCEE / HKDSE or above in any discipline;



Accurate and efficient input of data is a must;



Good typing skill (both Chinese and English);



Well organised, detail\\\\-minded, hardworking and highly responsible;



Familiar with Microsoft Excel functions and formulas is preferred; and



Immediately availability is highly preferred.



Remuneration will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. This position is offered on a temporary contract. For the successful candidate, future employment may be considered based on performance and organisational needs.



Interested parties please send your curriculum vitae stating the position (with reference number) you are applying for, current and expected salary, either by email to \\\\[email redacted, apply via Company website] or by mail to the Manager (Administration and Resources Management), The Property Management Services Authority, Units 806\\\\-8, 8/F, Dah Sing Financial Centre, 248 Queen’s Road East, Wan Chai, Hong Kong on or before 4 December 2025\\\\.



All information provided by applicants will be treated in strict confidence and used for recruitment purpose only.



Temporary

